Collapsed table borders: only the edges a cell actually draws

Upstream issue DioxusLabs/blitz#504, open with no fix as of 0.3.0-beta.2.

A computed border width keeps its value when the style is `none` or
`hidden` -- a borderless cell's width is still the initial `medium`,
3px. The collapsed model took that width for the grid's gutters and
painted them in the text colour, so every borderless layout table (most
newsletters) wore a 3px black grid and grew by its lines. Layout now
takes an edge's width as zero when its style draws nothing, and records
the per-edge widths on the TableContext; the painter draws each edge in
its own colour -- it used `border-top-color` for all four -- and skips an
edge that has no width or no visible colour.

Tested by crates/postio-render/tests/engine_patches.rs.

diff -ruN blitz-dom/src/layout/table.rs blitz-dom/src/layout/table.rs
